+# D10(b) place-overlap — the MOVER-MOVER arm (`f(!n, !n)`): moving the same
+# place twice in one call is the MAXIMAL place-overlap ("at most one writer OR
+# mover"). The self-host REJECTS it here with the overlap diagnostic.
+#
+# ⚠ SELF-HOST-TARGETED rejection test — NOT in the cross-compiler exact-code
+# conformance lane. Production Rust gg + ggdef reject the identical program one
+# pass EARLIER via `E_DoubleMove` (their move-tracker preempts place-overlap).
+# The self-host has NO upstream move-tracker yet (the liveness axis is a filed
+# HIGH track), so the faithful mirror of the FULL D10 rule lets this arm fire —
+# reject-with-a-different-code strictly beats ACCEPT. When the self-host
+# liveness pass lands it preempts this arm (ratified pass-order rider: liveness
+# precedes aliasing) and the diagnostic flips to the E_DoubleMove code. Owner
+# ruling "B2 SCOPE + LIVENESS-PASS" 2026-07-14.
+struct N:
+    Vector[int] data
+
+void f(N !a, N !b):
+    pass
+
+void run():
+    N n = N(Vector[int]())
+    f(!n, !n)
+
+void main():
+    run()
